{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782092763,"nonce":"954PsqQDcXSNE3bC3idnK828bRo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGOZ1mA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/307","origin":"github"},"title":"Add retrofit_sidescan_bag.py one-off tool to bizzyboat_project11/scripts/","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd a one-off bag-retrofit utility `retrofit_sidescan_bag.py` to `bizzyboat_project11/scripts/`.\n\nIt rewrites historical bizzy Garmin-sidescan bags (offline, into a NEW bag — input untouched) to carry:\n- **Radiometry** — `RawSonarImage.ping_info` `frequency` + `rx_beamwidths` (across-track fan) + `tx_beamwidths` (along-track), per channel, from the GCV-20 spec table. Bags captured before the driver populated these (marine_tools#62) have them empty.\n- **Geometry** — the three `tf_static` `garmin_sidescan→{port,starboard,down}` rotations patched to the measured **35° grazing tilt** (#305). Bags captured before #303/#305 carry the old horizontal (uncalibrated) boresight.\n\nEverything else passes through byte-for-byte; storage format + QoS preserved.\n\n## Why bizzyboat_project11 (not marine_tools)\n\nThis is **not needed by future users of the `garmin_sidescan` driver** — the driver now stamps beamwidths/frequency correctly (marine_tools#62), and new captures use the corrected URDF (#305). It's a one-off to make *legacy bizzy bags* reprocessable (mosaic / backscatter) with correct geometry + radiometry, so it lives with the bizzy platform.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `--grazing-deg` (default 35) and `--device gcv20|gcv10` are parameterized.\n- Fixes only the **static** mount frame; per-ping vessel roll lives in the bag's localization TF and composes correctly on reprocessing (#200).\n- Verified on field bags: side channels → 1.12 MHz / rx 55° / tx 0.44°, down → 820 kHz / rx 46° / tx 0.74°; port/stbd TF rotations → ∓125° (= ∓(90+35)).\n\nFollow-up to #305. Part of #185.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}